{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
The [G]first No[D]well
The [C]angel did [G]say
Was to [C]certain poor [G]shepherds
In [C]fields as they [D]lay;
In [G]fields where they [D]lay
[C]Keeping their [G]sheep,
On a [C]cold winter's [G]night
That [D]was so [G]deep.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
No[G]well, No[D]well,
No[C]well, No[G]well,
[Em]Born is the [C]King
Of [D]Isra[G]el.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
They [G]looked [D]up
And [C]saw a [G]star
[C]Shining in the [G]east
Be[C]yond them [D]far;
And [G]to the [D]earth
It [C]gave great [G]light,
And [C]so it con[G]tinued
Both [D]day and [G]night.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 3"}
And [G]by the [D]light
Of [C]that same [G]star
Three [C]wise men [G]came
From [C]country [D]far;
To [G]seek for a [D]king
[C]Was their in[G]tent,
And to [C]follow the [G]star
Wher[D]ever it [G]went.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
{x_end: G}
